#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Product naming (Habitat / Portal)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:12
msgid ""
"User-facing product terms (Chinese in [`i18n/glossary.md`](../../i18n/"
"glossary.md)):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Role | English | Chinese | Meaning |\n"
"| ---- | ------- | ------- | ------- |\n"
"| Long-running process / connect target | **Habitat** | **栖息地** | One process hosts **multiple digital lives** (`agent` subjects) and **human assets** (`user`); connect / token / restart target |\n"
"| External connectors (class) | **Portal** | **入口** | Shell, MCP clients, and similar ways in; not the Habitat itself |\n"
"| Shell | **Shell** | **壳** | A Portal (desktop / mobile / web window; SSH-like) |\n"
"| Admin / inspect UI (legacy Console) | **Habitat** (UI) | **栖息地** | \"Open Habitat\" vs \"Connect to Habitat\"; code routes may still say `console` |\n"
"| Admin home page | **Dashboard** | **仪表盘** | One page inside Habitat UI |\n"
"| Message bridges | **Gateway** | Gateway | Discord / WeChat — **not** a Portal |\n"
"| Wire / code legacy | **Hub** | — | Paths such as `/hub/rpc/v1`, `hubUrl`, `dev:hub` — keep until a migration task |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:24
msgid ""
"Verbs: **connect to Habitat** (URL + token); **open Habitat** (admin UI); "
"**reach via a Portal** (Shell / MCP)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:26
msgid ""
"Estate **Body** (VM / OS / network under the four-layer model) is the "
"cognitive \"what I run on\" for a subject — **not** the Habitat process name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hub configuration (SSOT)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:30
msgid ""
"User copy says Habitat; storage and RPC identifiers may still say `hub_*` "
"until migrated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer         | Storage                                                     | Who reads/writes                                          |\n"
"| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Bootstrap** | `~/.anima/config.yaml` (`database`, `http`, `redis`, `web`) | `platform/boot` only; install/ops edit YAML               |\n"
"| **Runtime**   | PostgreSQL `hub_runtime_config`                             | Engine, tools, Shell Habitat settings, Habitat UI `config.*` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:36 docs/concepts/memory.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Core Principles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:45
msgid ""
"The memory system may be layered internally, but the LLM sees a single entry "
"point"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:45
msgid ""
"Memory orchestration is built into the runtime; the LLM does not control "
"memory pipelines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:45
msgid "Credential management is a first-class system concern"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:45
msgid ""
"Habitat **runtime configuration** (LLM, compression, integrations) is "
"persisted in PostgreSQL (`hub_runtime_config`); `~/.anima/config.yaml` holds "
"**bootstrap** only (`database`, `http`, `redis`, `web`) for cold start — not "
"editable via Shell or Habitat UI API"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:45
msgid ""
"Habitat **may start without LLM** configured; first-time setup happens in "
"Shell **Settings → Habitat** (persist to PG), then restart Habitat so "
"registries rebuild. Missing `llm` must not block cold start."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:45
msgid ""
"Whether Habitat hosts browser `/web/*` is **`config.yaml` `web.enabled`** "
"(bootstrap; absent defaults to on when dist exists). Do not put this switch "
"in PG — empty runtime would otherwise block the Settings UI that configures "
"that runtime."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:45
msgid "**Asset management** is a first-class system concern"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:47
msgid ""
"Bootstrap and runtime are **not merged** into a single config object. CLI "
"cold paths connect via internal `withPlatformDb` and receive **runtime "
"only**. Legacy runtime keys in `config.yaml` are ignored (optional startup "
"warn)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:49
msgid ""
"The system prompt is part of architecture, not ad-hoc string concatenation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four Cognitive Layers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:53
msgid ""
"A digital life is structured from the inside out. Each layer answers a "
"different core question:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n"
"│ ① Consciousness                                │\n"
"│    \"What am I aware of right now?\"             │\n"
"│    The LLM runtime stream — the innermost now. │\n"
"│    Not persisted; flows and fades.             │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ② Self                                         │\n"
"│    \"Who am I?\"                                 │\n"
"│    └── existence_anchor (nearly immutable)     │\n"
"│    └── self_model (updatable)                   │\n"
"│    └── personality_baseline (semi-stable)       │\n"
"│    └── direction                                │\n"
"│    └── metacognition                            │\n"
"│    └── autobiography_summary (append-only)      │\n"
"│    See [`self-layer.md`](self-layer.md)        │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ③ Memory                                       │\n"
"│    \"What do I know / remember?\"                │\n"
"│    └── Semantic (incl. `procedural` type)      │\n"
"│    └── Episodic                                │\n"
"│    └── Limbic / Imprint                        │\n"
"│    See [`memory.md`](memory.md)                │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ④ Estate                                       │\n"
"│    \"What do I have / rely on?\"                  │\n"
"│    ├── Body: VM / OS / network / toolchains    │\n"
"│    │   (Estate cognitive body — not Habitat)   │\n"
"│    ├── Internal assets: notes, projects, code  │\n"
"│    └── External assets: email, accounts, creds│\n"
"│    Credentials: see \"Credential System\" below  │\n"
"└───────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer Relationships"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:94
msgid ""
"**Top-down dependency**: Consciousness content settles into Self; Self "
"decides what enters Memory; Memory and operational needs drive Estate "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:94
msgid ""
"**Self and Consciousness**: Consciousness is flowing awareness; Self is the "
"settled \"I\" distilled from it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:94
msgid ""
"**Self and Memory**: Self answers \"who am I\"; Memory answers \"what do I "
"know\". They are peers with different natures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:94
msgid ""
"**Estate** is outermost — not \"who I am\" but \"what I have and what I run "
"on\". Body and assets meet here as extensions of my boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unified entity storage (v0.8)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:98
msgid ""
"Structured business data (tasks, notes, email accounts/messages, future "
"memory migrations) converges on a single **`entities`** PostgreSQL table "
"with component tags (`task_list`, `task_item`, `email_account`, …). Self "
"layer [`self_blocks`](self-layer.md) stays physically separate. See [`entity-"
"model.md`](entity-model.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:100
msgid ""
"Shell UI **`/tasks`** and **`/email`** are primary module entries (entity-"
"backed); legacy Console email route removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anima URI (Shell locator)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:104
msgid ""
"Entity deep links / overlay / clipboard use **Anima URI** (`anima:{id}?"
"component=…&present=…`). Structured persistence still uses numeric entity "
"ids. See [`anima-uri.md`](anima-uri.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repository layout (Phase 0 — revised)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "Target layout is **feature modules** under `src/features/<slug>/` (UI + protocol + Hub adapter + domain + `plugin.ts`). Console is renamed **console** and uses the **same module shape** as chat/task — not a separate admin-\\* stack. `src/satellites/` is legacy naming; do not add new products there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "**End state:** Hub RPC per feature; business methods use `POST|WS /hub/rpc/v1` (same envelope). Public health/TLS probes and binary methods (e.g. `tts.synthesize`) are Hub RPC REST with `auth: optional` or Bearer as declared in registry.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:112
msgid "Authoritative spec: [`repository-topology.md`](repository-topology.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:114
msgid ""
"Engine stays horizontal: `src/kernel/`, `src/core/`, `src/runtime/`, `src/"
"platform/` (boot + routers). Shell host: `src/frontend/` (`ui-kit`, `shell-"
"sdk`, `shell-ui`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "Platform UI layering (legacy paths — migrating to features/\\*)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer            | Platform-native?                   | Location (current → target)                                            | 数据通道                                |\n"
"| ---------------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Shell（壳子维）  | Yes                                | `src/app/shell/desktop`, `src/app/shell/mobile`, companion, Hub wiring | preload/IPC                             |\n"
"| Shared SPA shell | 布局跟视口；设置 chrome 跟布局粗档 | `src/frontend/shell-ui`                                                | Hub RPC（Feature RPC）                  |\n"
"| Console 前端     | Shell embed                        | `src/features/console`（UI + `plugin.hub.rpc`）                        | Hub RPC（WS + HTTP POST `/hub/rpc/v1`） |\n"
"| 卫星应用         | Sidecar only                       | `src/satellites/companion`                                             | Hub RPC + SAP attach                    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:125
msgid ""
"导航与主布局**必须**用 `useLayoutMode()` / 视口断点（布局维），**禁止**用 "
"`isElectron` / `getShellKind()` 锁 Shell 布局。交互（右键/长按/Enter）用 "
"shell-sdk 交互 API。三维度标准 → [`.agent/rules/ui-dimensions.md`]"
"(../../.agent/rules/ui-dimensions.md)。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "**边界**：`shell-ui` 与 `src/features/*/ui` 通过 `shell-sdk` + Feature RPC 访问 Hub；**SAP attach / tool.\\*** 协议由 companion 等卫星 sidecar 使用。详见 [`.agent/rules/frontend-features.md`](../../.agent/rules/frontend-features.md)。\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:128
#, no-wrap
msgid "Console navigation ↔ cognitive layers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:131
msgid ""
"Console sidebar is grouped (not flat storage tables). Map new features onto "
"these user-visible concepts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Group        | Cognitive layer | Routes (representative)                             |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Runtime      | Estate + ops    | dashboard, config, cron                             |\n"
"| Memory       | Memory          | memory hub, browse sub-routes, sleep, auto-llm-runs |\n"
"| Self         | Self            | self-layer, system-prompt                           |\n"
"| Estate       | Estate          | subjects, worlds                                    |\n"
"| Capabilities | Estate (tools)  | tools, commands, mcp, acp, satellites               |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:141
msgid ""
"FTS index maintenance is under Memory (not top-level). Do not add new flat "
"nav items without mapping to a group above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:142 docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:145
msgid ""
"The four-layer model draws on cognitive psychology and the [Hindsight]"
"(https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.12818) four-network memory architecture, with "
"two fundamental extensions: limbic (emotional) memory and Estate (assets as "
"first-class citizens), plus Self split out from Memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "Situational Intelligence"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:149
msgid ""
"Where a digital life exists, how it exists, and what it may do — governed by "
"two independent but cooperating subsystems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scene Awareness"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:153
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: what kind of moment is this?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:155
msgid ""
"Scene awareness is **soft** — it adjusts tone, distance, memory recall bias, "
"and proactivity. It is not a permission system; it modulates presence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example dimensions (non-exhaustive):**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:161
msgid ""
"Topic: emotional / career / tech / philosophy / history / literature / daily "
"life"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:161
msgid "Activity: role-play / games / creation / programming / reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:161
msgid "Atmosphere: relaxed / focused / late night / intimate / urgent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operation:** Runs continuously without explicit switch commands. Inferred from dialogue, time, frequency, etc. See [`time-perception.md`](time-perception.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "Capability Mask"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:167
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: what tools and data can I use right now?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:169
msgid ""
"The capability mask is **hard** — it binds tool sets, data scope, and "
"credential permissions. The same digital life may wear different masks per "
"conversation or task to prevent permission leaks and tool pollution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:171
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example masks:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:178
msgid "Developer: terminal, code read/write, ACP Cursor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:178
msgid "Maintainer: FreeAnima config, deployment, database"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:178
msgid "Creator: files, notes, media generation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:178
msgid "Research: web search, paper retrieval"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:178
msgid "Role-play: dialogue context only, no external tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:178
msgid "Default: basic chat + limited lookup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operation:** Switches at conversation boundaries, explicit commands, or scene-awareness triggers. Each mask is a declared tool/data scope, not a separate identity.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "How They Interact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:183
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Scene awareness (soft tuning)\n"
"     │  tone, distance, recall bias\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"Capability mask (hard constraints)\n"
"     │  tools, permissions, data scope\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"Agent behavior\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:198
msgid ""
"Scene awareness infers \"what we are doing\" → may suggest mask switches and "
"presence adjustments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:198
msgid ""
"Capability mask constrains \"what I can do\" → prevents cross-scene tool "
"misuse"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:198
msgid "Both converge in final behavior but evolve independently"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:200
msgid ""
"For design drafts, open a GitHub Issue (no design-doc directory in docs)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "Memory Storage (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:209
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Cognitive type   | Description                                                                                 |\n"
"| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Episodic         | Conversation archive; full history retained                                                 |\n"
"| Semantic         | Cross-session facts, preferences, experiences; **`procedural` type** for \"how-to\" knowledge |\n"
"| Limbic           | Emotional anchors and imprints — \"what was felt\"                                            |\n"
"| Autobiographical | Meaning of important experiences; recalled on demand                                        |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:211
msgid ""
"Pipeline: nightly **sleep-cycle** pipeline (`builtin-sleep-cycle` cron) "
"extracts and maintains memory; `memory_recall` retrieves on demand during "
"chat. Details: [`memory.md`](memory.md), [`sleep.md`](sleep.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vault & Secrets (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:219
msgid ""
"**Vault** (ECS `vault_item` in User + Agent libraries) is the authoritative "
"secret store; legacy `~/.password-store` (pass) is **not deleted** on disk "
"but is no longer read at runtime"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:219
msgid ""
"The LLM **never sees secret values** — only vault item metadata and config "
"references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:219
msgid ""
"Runtime resolution: `vault(\"item_id\", \"field\")` and `env(\"KEY\")` in "
"config; Shell `/vault` for management"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:219
msgid "Secret values are not written to conversation archives or logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:219
msgid "CLI: `anima vault list|get`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:221
msgid "See [`guide/security.md`](../guide/security.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:222
#, no-wrap
msgid "Runtime Modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:225
msgid ""
"Production (standalone install CLI): `anima service` (systemd --user). Auto-"
"restarts after crashes; only `systemctl stop` stops the service. Source-tree "
"`anima` does **not** register `service` — use `bun run dev:hub` for local "
"Hub."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:228
msgid ""
"**hub / service**: long-running — Hub HTTP (`/hub/rpc/v1`), Discord / WeChat "
"Gateway, cron"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:228
msgid ""
"**UI**: `src/app/shell/desktop` / `src/app/shell/mobile` bundled SPA (Chat + "
"Console); Hub does not host `/console`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:229
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# standalone install\n"
"anima service start              # default: systemd --user (does not auto-build Web)\n"
"anima service start --foreground # foreground (logs to stdout; systemd unit uses this)\n"
"anima service status\n"
"\n"
"# monorepo / worktree\n"
"just dev                         # Hub (≥10000) + Vite Web (≥5000)\n"
"bun run dev:hub                  # Hub foreground (default random ≥10000; not 2658)\n"
"bun run dev:web                  # browser shell Vite HMR from :5000 (set FREEANIMA_URL)\n"
"bun run build:web                # source deploy / Hub /web: build dist before start\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:242
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Architecture (Three Layers)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:245
msgid ""
"Tools are registered in three layers but exposed to the LLM as one **flat "
"tool list**. The LLM cares about names and parameters, not origin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:246
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"LLM view — flat tool list:\n"
"  file_read_file(path)           ← local\n"
"  file_write_file(path, content) ← local\n"
"  code_execute(code)             ← local\n"
"  query_database(sql)            ← MCP server\n"
"  send_email(to, subject)        ← MCP server\n"
"  acp_cursor(goal, context)      ← ACP agent\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 1: Local Tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:260
msgid "Execute inside the FreeAnima process; lowest latency"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:260
msgid "Registered automatically at service startup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 2: MCP Tools (Model Context Protocol)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:266
msgid "Connect to external MCP servers (separate processes)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:266
msgid ""
"Each server may register many fine-grained tools (single function calls)"
msgstr ""

